# ============================================================
# AFI LISTEN BACKEND — PROJECT RULES (Cursor / Copilot / Any AI)
# ============================================================
# These rules are MANDATORY. Every generated file must comply.
# Non-compliant code must be refused or rewritten immediately.
# ============================================================

## 🧱 STACK LOCKED

- Runtime : Node.js 18+, Express 5 (latest stable), TypeScript (strict).
- Prisma 7.x : 
  - ALWAYS use Driver Adapters (`@prisma/adapter-pg` + `pg`).
  - NEVER use `url` in `schema.prisma`. Use `prisma.config.ts`.
  - Re-generate client after any schema change (`npx prisma generate`).
- BullMQ 5.x : For background jobs (requires `maxRetriesPerRequest: null`).
- Zod : MANDATORY for ALL validations (body, params, query).
- Auth : JWT (jsonwebtoken) + bcrypt.
- DB : PostgreSQL via Supabase.

## 📁 FOLDER ARCHITECTURE — IMMUTABLE

```
src/
 ├── modules/
 │    ├── auth/            → controller, service, schema, route, types
 │    ├── reports/         → controller, service, schema, route, types
 │    ├── evaluations/     → controller, service, schema, route, types
 │    ├── ai/              → controller, service, schema, route, types
 │    ├── decisions/       → controller, service, schema, route, types
 │
 ├── core/
 │    ├── config/          → env.ts (typed), queue.ts, redis.ts
 │    ├── database/        → prisma.ts (adapter-based singleton)
 │    ├── middleware/      → auth.middleware.ts, error.middleware.ts, validate.middleware.ts
 │    ├── errors/          → AppError.ts
 │
 ├── jobs/
 │    ├── ai.processor.ts  → BullMQ Worker — ALL AI calls go here
 │
 ├── utils/                → pure helpers (pagination, response, etc.)
 │
 ├── app.ts                → Express app setup
 ├── server.ts             → HTTP server entrypoint
```

## 🔐 MODULE STRUCTURE — PER MODULE

Every module MUST have exactly these files:

```
modules/<name>/
  ├── <name>.controller.ts   → calls service, returns ApiResponse
  ├── <name>.service.ts      → business logic, calls repository
  ├── <name>.repository.ts   → Prisma calls only
  ├── <name>.schema.ts       → Zod schemas
  ├── <name>.route.ts        → Express router + validation middleware
  └── <name>.types.ts        → TS interfaces for the module
```

## ⚙️ EXPRESS 5 RULES

- **Params Typing** : Always cast `req.params.id as string` (Express 5 types params as `string | string[]`).
- **Async Handling** : native support for async errors, no need for `express-async-errors`.
- **Response Format** : Always use `{ success: boolean, message: string, data: any, error: any }`.

## ⚙️ CONTROLLER RULES

- Receives request → Validates (via middleware) → Calls Service → Returns ApiResponse.
- ZERO business logic.
- ZERO Prisma calls.
- ZERO AI calls.

## ⚙️ SERVICE RULES

- Orchestrates logic, calls repositories, enqueues jobs.
- ZERO Express types (`Request`, `Response`).
- AI tasks: ALWAYS enqueue a BullMQ job, NEVER call AI API inline.
- Stateless and strictly typed.

## ⚙️ REPOSITORY RULES

- Only Prisma CRUD operations.
- No business logic.

## ⚙️ PRISMA / DB RULES

- Singleton client in `src/core/database/prisma.ts`.
- Use `@prisma/adapter-pg` for direct connections.
- Migrations only via `npx prisma migrate`.

## 📝 CODE STYLE

- TypeScript strict: `noImplicitAny`, `strictNullChecks` ON.
- No `any` type — use `unknown` if necessary.
- Named exports preferred.

## 📌 SCRIPTS (package.json)

```json
{
  "dev": "nodemon -w src -e ts --exec \"ts-node src/server.ts\"",
  "build": "tsc",
  "start": "node dist/server.js"
}
```
